==============================================================================================
 HEPTAGON TOURNAMENTS: minimal-flip depth to transitive = MIN FEEDBACK ARC SET
==============================================================================================

 R_7 rotational {1,2,3}:
   #3-cycles=14  Ham-paths(H)=175  |Aut|=7
   base-ordering 0->..->6 back-arcs (opus's flipped tiles) = 6
   TRUE MIN FEEDBACK ARC SET (min back-arcs over all 7! orders) = 6  (best order (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6))
   => opus's 6 is the BASE count; the metagraph geodesic to transitive is MFAS=6 = phi(14)=6 (atom count)!

 Paley_7 QR {1,2,4}:
   #3-cycles=14  Ham-paths(H)=189  |Aut|=21
   base-ordering 0->..->6 back-arcs (opus's flipped tiles) = 7
   TRUE MIN FEEDBACK ARC SET (min back-arcs over all 7! orders) = 7  (best order (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6))
   => opus's 6 is the BASE count; the metagraph geodesic to transitive is MFAS=7 (NOT 6; base count 6 is not minimal)

==============================================================================================
 R_7 <-> Paley_7 minimal flip distance, and to transitive
==============================================================================================
   flip_dist(R_7, Paley_7) = 5  (metagraph geodesic between the two heptagon classes)
   MFAS(R_7)=6, MFAS(Paley_7)=7  (depth of each below transitive)

 INTERPRET: MFAS = the minimal-flip metagraph depth; opus's '6 tiles' is the base-labeling Hamming
   weight, an UPPER bound on the geodesic. The true depth is the feedback-arc-set invariant.
DONE.
